@dleach02 - please rebase and add the commit from #79884 to your pr (suggested by @nashif)

> a hotfix needs to be straightforward, no discussion, no change requests, no doubts about the change being made, when someone thinks a hotfix deserves a NACK, the rest of us can't wait for this conversation to conclude. Just include the reverted patch into that PR and work your way through this, probably it is going to be the same outcome with main branch less broken at that time.

Thanks for the fix

> The full path is not needed when the required file is in the same directory as the requesting file. There are only two cases which need to be addressed here; those where a file in posix/sys refers to a file in posix/ The alternative solution would be to add "../" to the existing reference, and that would ensure that the correct file was selected as the current directory is always searched first for "" include references.

@keith-packard I was aware that the full path is not needed and the distinction between "" and <> but at the late hour I felt it was just being consistent to change them all and do the <>. I can do the "../" if that is what you desire.

But maybe @cfriedt can redo his original patch to do this as I thought his patch was needed to fix another hotfix problem?
